# English for code, Spanish for UI

## Always in English (new files and symbols)

- File and folder names: `ProductReviewsSection.tsx`, `shopFilters.ts`, `banner/`
- Components, functions, hooks, types, variables, props
- Comments and commit messages (unless the team explicitly uses Spanish for commits)
- Route segment folder names under `src/app` when you create new ones (prefer English slugs for code; existing Spanish routes like `/about/como-hacer-un-reclamo` are legacy — do not rename without a product request)

## Spanish is allowed only for user-facing content

- Labels, headings, placeholders, error messages shown in the browser
- SEO titles/descriptions aimed at Colombian/Spanish-speaking customers
- Static copy in `about/` info pages

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD
export function ShopSortBar({ onSortChange }: ShopSortBarProps) {
  return <button aria-label="Ordenar productos">Precio: menor a mayor</button>;
}

// ❌ BAD — Spanish symbol names
export function BarraOrdenTienda() { ... }
const obtenerProductosDestacados = async () => { ... };
```

## Naming conventions

| Kind | Convention | Example |
|------|------------|---------|
| React components | PascalCase | `ProductCard.tsx` |
| Hooks | `use` + PascalCase | `useGoogleAuth.ts` |
| Utils / lib | camelCase | `groupedCatalog.ts`, `reviewUtils.ts` |
| Folders | lowercase English | `catalog/`, `reviews/` |
| Types | PascalCase | `ProductCardData`, `SessionUser` |
